fact WorkItem(id: "WI-670", description: some(value: "Floundered rule-goal counted as a solution in default resolve mode, bypassing hard-failing conjuncts. The open-time whole-body caller-var pre-check (body_builtins_delay_on_caller_vars_nodes, resolve.rs ~5879, feeding the delay-propagation gate at resolve.rs ~2310) delays the ENTIRE rule before its body opens whenever any body builtin's first positional arg resolves to an unbound CALLER var — so earlier hard-failing conjuncts (a 0-candidate fact lookup; a Failure-returning builtin like scope() on _global) never run to refute the branch. The residualization gate (resolve.rs ~756-775) then yields the still-delayed rule-goal as a NON-DEFINITE Solution (residual = [the rule goal]) under the default definite_only:false, so kb.resolve() reports a SPURIOUS solution. Repro (found during WI-630): rule entity_of(?x,?sort) :- nonvar(?x), EntityInfo(name:?x), scope(?x,?sort), kind(?sort,\"Sort\") — querying entity_of(Color,?s) for a top-level sort Color (no EntityInfo(name:Color) fact; scope(Color)=_global fails) returns 1 solution with ?s UNBOUND, instead of 0. Removing the trailing kind(?sort,...) builtin → correct 0, because then no body builtin delays on a caller var and the pre-check lets the body open so EntityInfo/scope refute the branch. WI-630 worked around it by keeping the guard's FIRST arg bound (is_entity_of(?x,?sort), ?x bound → pre-check does not flag it). ADJACENT-BUT-DISTINCT: WI-519 [R] residual-honesty bites in definite_only contexts (guards/quantifiers/NAF), NOT the default kb.resolve path; WI-322/WI-504 are the pre-check UNDER-detecting caller vars (opposite class). This is the OVER-eager whole-rule delay + residual-counted-as-solution in DEFAULT mode. FIX OPTIONS (STOP-AND-ASK, touches core SLD delay/residual semantics): (a) extend the WI-519 residual-honesty backstop to the default kb.resolve path — a rule-goal residual left ONLY by the open-time pre-check must not count as a definite solution (drop or flag it); (b) before flouncing the whole rule at the pre-check, verify the rule's non-delayed conjuncts are individually satisfiable first. Acceptance: the repro returns 0; existing delay-and-rotate legit cases (entity_of enumeration mode, computational rule bodies eq(?v, expr)) stay green; cargo-test green. SCOPE: resolver, Rust-only."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-07-16T08:09:23Z"))

fact Feedback(workitem: "WI-670", author: "user", content: "DELIVERED (2026-07-16), commit 43c21e11, full workspace suite green (79 binaries, 0 failed), /code-review xhigh done (no correctness bugs). Chose neither option (a) nor (b) verbatim but their sound refinement: at the open-time whole-rule delay pre-check, before delaying the rule on a caller var, run body_refuted_by_ground_conjunct over the freshly-opened body and DROP the candidate (StepResult::Continue) if any non-builtin conjunct with a concrete functor has ZERO non-equation discrim candidates under the head-match subst. query_view over-approximates + KB fixed during resolution => zero candidates is a hard fact no later var binding can reverse, so this never drops a satisfiable rule (sound under NAF). This is stricter/cheaper than option (b)'s 'individually satisfiable' (only refutes on a hard 0-candidate, never speculatively delays), and unlike option (a) it fixes the bug at the SOURCE rather than filtering residuals downstream (an honest stuck-builtin residual and an honest delayed-but-satisfiable rule residual both still count).\n\nKEY LANDMINES handled: refutation DISABLED for every resolution path query_view can't see — assumed_facts (WI-108) / gamma overlay (WI-537) / [simp] folded into context_opaque at the SearchStream caller (KnowledgeBase has no config); and per-functor route_handler_for (external rows), bare_bodied_bool_relation (routed to eq(f(args),true), WI-580), and scoping/quantifier markers forall_impl/forall_in/some_in/__pop_assumption — each a 0-candidate goal step_init nonetheless resolves, so treating it as refuted would FALSELY refute. Marker names extracted into shared is_scoping_marker_name so step_init's marker dispatch and the refutation skip can't drift. Note context_opaque lives on SearchStream/ResolveConfig, not KnowledgeBase (E0609 during impl).\n\nREGRESSION guard tests/wi670_floundered_rule_test.rs (3): dead rule (refuting conjunct) => 0 solutions; stuck builtin nonvar(?s) alone => 1 residual (kept); honest delayed rule check(?x):-nonvar(?x),is_thing(name:?x) with fact is_thing(name:\"hello\") => 1 residual (kept — the case a naive 'drop any un-opened rule-goal residual' fix, my first (a) attempt, wrongly discarded and which broke delay_propagation_residualizes_when_unresolvable). WI-630's workaround (keep the guard's FIRST arg bound) is no longer required for CORRECTNESS.", at: "2026-07-16T08:10:03Z")
